---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout title="Sandvik Hydraulic Quick Couplers | Hydraulic Quick Couplings" description="Hydraulic quick couplers for Sandvik machines — ISO 7241 / ISO 16028 flat-face / ISO 5675 profiles, sizes, threads and selection notes for Sandvik fleets.">
  <section class="bg-navy-950 text-white">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-4 py-16 sm:px-6">
      <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-night-green">Machine-Compatible Quick Couplings</p>
      <h1 class="mt-2 max-w-3xl text-4xl font-extrabold tracking-tight">Sandvik Hydraulic Quick Couplers</h1>
      <p class="mt-3 max-w-2xl text-lg text-slate-300">Source the right quick-disconnect couplings for Sandvik machines — attachment lines, implement outlets and service replacements.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="bg-white">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-4 py-16 sm:px-6">
      <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none prose-headings:font-extrabold prose-headings:text-navy-950 prose-h2:mt-10 prose-p:text-slate-600 prose-a:text-brand-blue">
        <h2>Sandvik Machines and Their Hydraulic Quick Couplings</h2>
        <p>Sandvik builds mining and rock-excavation equipment — drills, crushers, loaders and underground machines. Sandvik mining equipment runs high-pressure hydraulic circuits that commonly use flat-face (ISO 16028 style) or heavy-duty ISO 7241 ball-lock couplings; pressure ratings matter more than on standard mobile gear.</p>
        <h2>Coupling Profiles You Will Find on Sandvik Equipment</h2>
        <p>The table below summarises the quick-coupling profiles most commonly used across Sandvik machine families. It is a field guide, not a guarantee: verify the profile on your specific machine before ordering.</p>
        <table>
          <thead><tr><th>Machine family</th><th>Common profile</th><th>Typical sizes</th><th>Typical threads</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td>Drilling rigs</td><td>Flat-face (ISO 16028 style)</td><td>1/2&quot; - 3/4&quot;</td><td>ORFS / metric</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Loaders / underground machines</td><td>Ball-lock ISO 7241</td><td>1/2&quot; - 1"</td><td>ORFS / NPT</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Service lines</td><td>Ball-lock ISO 7241</td><td>1/2&quot; - 1"</td><td>ORFS / NPT</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
        <h2>Selection Notes for Sandvik Fleets</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Sandvik mining equipment runs high-pressure circuits — match the coupling pressure rating, not just the profile.</li><li>Drilling rigs commonly use flat-face couplings for low-spill connection.</li><li>Threads are often ORFS or metric on mining equipment; confirm per machine.</li>
        </ul>
        <h2>Replacement and Service Guidance</h2>
        <p>For Sandvik machines, provide the pressure rating of the circuit with the coupling request — mining circuits exceed standard mobile ratings, and the coupling must be specified accordingly.</p>
        <h2>FAQ</h2>
        <h3>What couplings do Sandvik machines use?</h3><p>Sandvik mining equipment uses flat-face (ISO 16028 style) on drills and ISO 7241 ball-lock on loaders — always confirm pressure rating.</p><h3>Do Sandvik machines use special couplings?</h3><p>Profiles are standard, but the pressure rating must match the mining circuit — specify pressure when ordering.</p><h3>What threads on Sandvik equipment?</h3><p>ORFS and metric threads are common on mining equipment; confirm per machine.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="bg-slate-50">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-4 py-16 sm:px-6">
      <div class="flex flex-col items-center justify-between gap-6 rounded-2xl bg-navy-950 p-8 text-center sm:p-10 lg:flex-row lg:text-left">
        <div>
          <h3 class="text-2xl font-extrabold text-white">Need Couplings for Sandvik Machines?</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-slate-300">Send the machine model, coupling profile or a photo — we confirm the match within 24 hours.</p>
        </div>
        <a href="/contact/" class="rounded-lg bg-cta-orange px-6 py-3 font-semibold text-white transition hover:bg-orange-600">Request a Quote</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
